CM_ BO_ 2015 "OBD-II functional request, tester -> all ECUs. A Mode-01 read is the three bytes 02 01 <PID> padded to 8. Send at no more than about 20 requests/s - this vehicle was polled at ~85 ms per PID with no dropped replies.";
CM_ BO_ 2016 "Physical request to the ECM. Used for UDS ReadDataByIdentifier (03 22 F1 90 = VIN) and for the ISO-TP flow-control frame (30 00 00) that a multi-frame reply requires. NOTE: this vehicle IGNORES OBD-II Mode 09 PID 02 and KWP 1A 90 - UDS 22 F190 on this address is the only VIN path that answered.";
CM_ BO_ 2024 "ECM response. This vehicle broadcasts NOTHING on its OBD-2 port - every frame here exists only because the tester asked. The ECM reports 33 supported PIDs; 20 were confirmed answering and 11 more are claimed but untested. See docs/SUZUKI_DZIRE_2026_GATEWAY.md.";
CM_ BO_ 2030 "Second module. Answers only PIDs 01, 21, 30, 31 and 42. It reports its OWN DistanceSinceCodesCleared (5217 km) and voltage, which differ from the ECM (5214 km) - key responses by responder ID or two constants will look like one varying signal.";
CM_ SG_ 2024 MonitorStatus "CONFIRMED: this ECU answered it in the 2026-08-20 capture.";
CM_ SG_ 2024 FuelSystemStatus "CLAIMED: the ECU lists it in its supported-PID bitmap but it was never polled in the capture, so the response is untested.";
